#* {{quote-book|en|year=1945|title=Origins from mythology of biological names and terms|author=Patrick Henry Yancey|pages=46}}
#*: Two kinds were on the market: ''Unicornum Verum'' ('''Alicorn'''), thought to be Mammoth Tusk, and ''Unicornum Falsum'', Narwhal tusks.
