===Etymology 2===
Term already associated with unicorns and reinterpreted as a blend of {{der|en|la|āla|t=wing}} with ''unicorn'', popularized by ''Bearing an Hourglass'' (1984) and other fantasy novels by Piers Anthony.<ref>[http://mlp.wikia.com/wiki/User_blog:Nathan2000/Winged_unicorns According to Nathan2000], when asked how he came up with the term, Anthony answered, “I saw fantasy statuettes in an ad, and one was of a winged unicorn, titled an alicorn, so I figured that was the name and used it. I have not been able to verify it elsewhere.”</ref>

